-- All men are mortal; Socrates is a man; so Socrates is mortal. Facts and
-- a rule as clauses of one family. The rule applies the family again, so
-- `is` is compiled as a word of its own, which tests its symbols as it
-- runs.

is: < Socrates Human > [ drop drop true ] ;
is: < Plato Human > [ drop drop true ] ;
is: < x Mortal > [ drop Human is ] ;
is: < x y > [ drop drop false ] ;

Socrates Mortal is Zeus Mortal is Plato Human is
